A. Parameters (SIMULATED, illustrative)
failure probability per trade p = 1/8
cost per business day of delay kappa = 2500 cents
delays ell_1, ell_2, ell_3 = (1, 2, 4) business days
B. Independent failures: each fail pattern, with its probability and cost
pattern (ok ok ok): probability 343/512, cost 0 cents
pattern (ok ok fail): probability 49/512, cost 10000 cents
pattern (ok fail ok): probability 49/512, cost 5000 cents
pattern (ok fail fail): probability 7/512, cost 15000 cents
pattern (fail ok ok): probability 49/512, cost 2500 cents
pattern (fail ok fail): probability 7/512, cost 12500 cents
pattern (fail fail ok): probability 7/512, cost 7500 cents
pattern (fail fail fail): probability 1/512, cost 17500 cents
probabilities sum to one: True
expected cost by enumeration: 4375/2 cents
closed form p * kappa * sum of delays: 4375/2 cents
enumeration equals closed form: True
closed form rounded half up to the cent: 2188 cents
probability that no trade fails: 343/512
probability that at least one trade fails: 169/512
three times p, for comparison: 3/8
probability that at least one trade fails is below three times p: True
C. Equal delays of 2 business days for each trade
expected cost by enumeration: 1875 cents
closed form 3 * p * kappa * ell: 1875 cents
enumeration equals 3 * p * kappa * ell: True
D. Same marginal probability, two joint laws: no-cost probability, mean and variance
comonotone: probability of no cost 7/8, mean 4375/2 cents, variance 133984375/4 square cents
independent: probability of no cost 343/512, mean 4375/2 cents, variance 57421875/4 square cents
the two means are equal: True
the comonotone variance is larger: True
